course: dictionary
lesson: 15285
title: Sinful: serious or silly?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have a serious meaning and a silly meaning. «Sinful» is one of them. In church and Bible lessons, it means wrong according to God's law or religious teaching. «The priest said that lying and stealing were sinful acts, and he asked people to ask for forgiveness.» The clues forgiveness and asking for forgiveness show the serious meaning.
explain: In jokes and everyday talk, sinful means very naughty, or too much of something good. «These sinfully rich brownies are so gooey that I had three before lunch.» Nobody means that the brownies broke God's law here. The speaker is joking that the brownies are so tempting they feel a bit naughty to eat.
explain: To work out which meaning is right, look at the topic around the word. Church, prayer and forgiveness point to the serious meaning. Food, treats and fun point to the joking meaning. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Sinful is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a person, an action or a thing.
fact: «Sinful» means wrong according to God's law or religious teaching, or full of sin.
fact: In a joke, «sinful» means very naughty, or too much, as in «a sinful dessert».
fact: «Sinfully delicious» means so tasty that it almost feels naughty to eat.
fact: Look at the topic around the word: forgiveness points to the serious meaning, and treats or food point to the joking one.
exercise: «The priest said that lying and stealing were sinful acts.» What does sinful mean here? | Very tasty | Very loud | *Wrong according to God's law or religious teaching | Very funny
exercise: «The sinfully rich chocolate cake was gone in five minutes.» What does sinfully mean here? | *So tempting and rich that it feels a bit naughty | Very slow | Cold and wet | Wrong in a court of law
exercise: «He asked God to forgive his sinful thoughts.» Which word in the sentence shows that sinful has its serious meaning? | cake | *forgive | sunny | laughed
test: Ben says, «The pizza was sinfully good.» Which meaning fits best? | Full of sin in a religious way, so Ben is sorry | *Very tasty, so good it feels a little naughty | Cooked badly and cold | Very quiet and slow
test: Which word could replace sinful in «a sinful dessert» without losing the joking feel? | sleepy | empty | *very naughty and tempting | cheap
exam: Which sentence uses sinful in the serious, religious sense? | «The sinful puppy ate my homework.» | «The sinful brownies were gone before lunch.» | *«The monk prayed for forgiveness for his sinful deeds.»
